# Program matching

`matchesFilters(program, filters, options)` in `src/js/modules/filters.js` is the single decision point for whether a program appears in results. It takes its helpers via the `options` object (dependency injection) rather than reaching for globals, so it stays testable — keep it that way.

`src/js/modules/search.js` parses free-text queries into structured filters (`parseSmartSearch`), which are then fed into `matchesFilters` alongside the dropdown values.

## Location matching

`programServesLocation` in `src/js/utils/location-match.js` accepts a match on **any** of these — it is a union, not a conjunction:

1. Direct city match on any of the program's locations (fuzzy-matched)
2. The search city's county matches `service_area.counties`, `primary_county`, or a location's `county`
3. The program has an in-person site in the same county as the search city
4. Broad regional coverage — `Multiple`, `North Texas`, `Dallas County`, `National`
5. The program is virtual/telehealth
6. Org/program/notes text mentions a DFW-area keyword

City normalization handles the DeSoto/De Soto split and en/em dashes. Add new cities to `CITY_TO_COUNTY` there, not to a caller.

## Age semantics

`programServesAge` returns `true`, `false`, or **`null`**. `null` means `ages_served` was unparseable, and it must **not** exclude the program — only an explicit `false` filters it out. Writing `if (!serves)` instead of `if (serves === false)` silently drops valid programs.

## Feature-flag gates

Several filters only run when the matching flag in `src/js/config/constants.js` is on:

- `STATEWIDE_MODE` — **off in production**; gates county filtering
- `SHOW_SUD_FILTERS` — gates `service_domain` and `sud_services`
- `SHOW_VERIFICATION_FILTERS` — gates the verification-recency filter

The SUD-services filter additionally only applies when `serviceDomain` is also `substance_use`, mirroring the UI where those checkboxes are nested under that domain. A test that sets SUD services without setting the domain exercises nothing and passes vacuously.

## Crisis visibility

Crisis listings are excluded from normal treatment results and only surface via the crisis toggle or a crisis preset. 988 remains the primary crisis path — don't elevate directory crisis entries above it.

## Testing this code

`scripts/validate-filters.js` imports the real `matchesFilters` and `parseSmartSearch` rather than reimplementing them; `npm run validate-filters` runs during every build. If you change matching behavior, verify the suite actually fails when you break the real logic — a suite that tests a copy can pass while production is broken.
